      "text": "When an idea matters, a smaller commitment can seem to understate enthusiasm. Finding that 'I can do this much' sounds smaller than the interest behind it, promising more may become a way of trying to show how much one cares.",
      "facts": ["S1", "C1", "I1", "C2", "I2"],
      "scenes": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Consider transiting Jupiter's trine to natal Mars as a lengthening stride, with transiting Saturn's square to natal Sun as the pack that comes along; a faster pace does not make the pack lighter. While expansion can increase the structure needed, enthusiasm and the scope of a promise can be expressed separately.",
      "facts": ["S1", "C1", "I1", "C2", "I2"],
      "scenes": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Before adding a piece of work, one can distinguish wanting that work from wanting the promise to express enthusiasm. The size of a commitment need not carry all the expression of interest.",
      "facts": ["S1", "C1", "I1", "C2", "I2"],
      "scenes": []
    }
  ]
